---
import DocsPage from "../../layouts/DocsPage.astro"

export const prerender = true
---

<DocsPage id="models">

          <p>
            Connect a provider account or API key to start. Eligible accounts may also see Free models inside of
            Vector, with availability and usage limits shown in the app.
          </p>

          <h2 id="byok">Bring your own key</h2>
          <p>
            Connect a provider in Settings, or run <code>vector providers login</code> in the terminal, then
            select a model in the session composer. Model availability, context limits, pricing, and
            rate limits come from the provider. Vector's usage view tracks the information returned by
            those sessions.
          </p>
          <p class="note">
            The upcoming release no longer loads the former third-party hosted providers, even with an API key.
            Choose another provider before starting a task. Sign in with ChatGPT stays available for OpenAI models. Native
            Copilot, xAI, GitLab OAuth, Poe and DigitalOcean sign-in flows are paused pending Vector's own registrations;
            API-key methods remain where supported.
            External Claude Code, Codex,
            and Cursor runtimes still use your own installed CLIs and their authentication.
          </p>

          <h2 id="free-models">Free models inside of Vector</h2>
          <p>
            The upcoming release adds a section for approved OpenRouter free models when the service is enabled.
            Sign in to Vector for a shared allowance, or choose Connect OpenRouter to use your own account directly.
            Each model identifies its source: Shared Vector allowance or Your OpenRouter account.
            When both offer the same model, your account takes precedence. The section is hidden when the service is off.
          </p>
          <p>
            Uses your own free OpenRouter account: 50 requests a day, or 1,000 if you've ever added $10 of OpenRouter credits.
            OpenRouter supplies this free access; Vector does not charge for, provide, or pay for these tokens.
            When the shared allowance is exhausted, Vector shows its expected reset time and lets you connect OpenRouter
            to continue the same conversation. Workspace subscription terms are unchanged.
          </p>
          <p>
            Prompts are processed by OpenRouter and the selected model provider. Retention and training policies vary
            by provider; review those policies before sending confidential code. This describes upcoming functionality,
            not an announcement that the shared service is enabled in production.
          </p>

          <h2 id="cli-models">Models in the terminal</h2>
          <p>
            <code>vector models</code> lists the supported model catalog. Connect a provider with <code>vector providers login</code> to use its models. Pass a provider id to filter and <code>--verbose</code> for metadata such as per-token cost. The catalog is bundled with the release. From 1.99.91, the next release, <code>--refresh</code> only fetches when a mirror is explicitly configured with <code>VECTOR_MODELS_URL</code>, <code>VECTOR_MODELS_PATH</code> selects a local catalog, and <code>VECTOR_DISABLE_MODELS_FETCH=1</code> disables refresh.
          </p>
          <p class="doc-cmd"><code>vector models
vector models anthropic --verbose</code><button class="doc-cmd-copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy this command">Copy</button></p>
          <p>
            In the upcoming release, an enabled service adds the heading <strong>Free models inside of Vector</strong>,
            with shared allowance or own OpenRouter account captions. Display names omit <code>:free</code>;
            selectors retain it. Your account takes precedence over a duplicate shared model. Human guidance goes
            to stderr, while stdout keeps plain model selectors. Connect your own account with
            <code>vector providers login --provider openrouter --method "Connect OpenRouter"</code>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Models that expose reasoning effort take <code>--variant</code>. The level resolves from the flag, then your saved preference, then what the session last used, and your choice is kept per provider and model.
          </p>
</DocsPage>
